Alembic — Crop Care Crop
========================

Every schema change is a migration file in `alembic/versions/`.
The database URL is injected by `env.py` from DATABASE_URL (see .env.example).

Typical workflow
----------------
# 1. Change `app/models/*.py`
# 2. Generate a migration
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"

# 3. READ the generated file in alembic/versions/ — edit if needed
# 4. Apply it
alembic upgrade head

Useful inspection commands
--------------------------
alembic current              # which revision is applied
alembic history --verbose    # full timeline
alembic upgrade head --sql   # emit SQL without running it (offline mode)

Never edit an applied migration. Create a new one instead.
